## Architecture (sustainable)
- **Coexistence, one implementation:** IPC handlers stay registered; bodies now
  delegate to new electron-free stores in `@slayzone/task/server`
  (artifact-store, template-store, events/taskEvents, artifact-watcher emitter).
  Both transports call the same code. No renderer cutover / handler deletion (slice 5).
- **task CRUD/deps/board ops injected** into transport via `setTaskDeps()` (they're
  electron-coupled: createTaskOp → @slayzone/worktrees/main → electron) — same
  pattern as chat/integrations. artifacts/template stores are electron-free → imported
  directly. `OpDeps.ipcMain` made optional (`ipcMain?.emit`) so ops run from tRPC with `{}`.
- **Download dialogs** extracted to `@slayzone/task/main/artifact-downloads` (Electron-only),
  shared by IPC + router (no duplicated tree-walk/zip logic).
- **artifact-watcher**: typed `artifactWatcherEvents` emitter (electron-free); `/main`
  bridges it to `BrowserWindow.send('artifacts:content-changed')` for renderer coexistence.

